{"title":"2021 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Area_of_Circles_and_Logic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Area of Circles and Logic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a plane, four circles with radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ead07d014eac1a900adbbed052e5beabc41aa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,3,5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are tangent to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> at the same point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c1e22fe09c7388d738ebd1e52fb999e0eae620f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> but they may be on either side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />. Region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> consists of all the points that lie inside exactly one of the four circles. What is the maximum possible area of region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63b09639c75431bb8ff941562dee769bcc54712a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }24\\pi \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }32\\pi \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }64\\pi \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }65\\pi \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }84\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"453\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> is horizontal, and each circle lies either north or south to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d87b9e52f73f40ab2bfe4ab08cb9516a230bb8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> We construct the circles one by one:\n</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-left: 1.5em;\">\n  <li>Without the loss of generality, we draw the circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> north to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d87b9e52f73f40ab2bfe4ab08cb9516a230bb8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /></li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li>To maximize the area of region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2e8e8dd78b26ddc9ac278cc179101d30644cae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"16\" /> we draw the circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> south to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d87b9e52f73f40ab2bfe4ab08cb9516a230bb8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /></li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li>Now, we need to subtract the circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <i><b>at least</b></i>. The optimal situation is that the circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> encompasses the circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf27edd6ee0c25241392922eca9b9c9144f4d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> in which we do not need to subtract more. That is, the two smallest circles are on the same side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93fcfdc078ee323f68acac829385319761da334a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"11\" height=\"16\" /> but can be on either side. </li>\n</ol>\n<p>The diagram below shows one possible configuration of the four circles:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/09622ff57f1014e51375086c90e7e2cf7dd463c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* diagram made by samrocksnature, edited by MRENTHUSIASM */ pair A=(10,0); pair B=(-10,0); draw(A--B); filldraw(circle((0,7),7),yellow); filldraw(circle((0,-5),5),yellow); filldraw(circle((0,-3),3),white); filldraw(circle((0,-1),1),white); dot((0,0)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,0),(0,1.5)); label(&quot;$\\ell$&quot;,(10,0),(1.5,0)); [/asy]\" width=\"228\" height=\"252\" />\nTogether, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/0/12085f7773e6077355a9d89c52960c9af327c11f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi\\cdot7^2+\\pi\\cdot5^2-\\pi\\cdot3^2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }65\\pi}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"270\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~samrocksnature ~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Area_of_Circles_and_Logic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Area_of_Circles_and_Logic)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Area of Circles and Logic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Area of Circles and Logic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/yPIFmrJvUxM\">https://youtu.be/yPIFmrJvUxM</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GYpAm8v1h-U?t=206\">https://youtu.be/GYpAm8v1h-U?t=206</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DvpN56Ob6Zw?t=555\">https://youtu.be/DvpN56Ob6Zw?t=555</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3jC_yOKA7xE\">https://youtu.be/3jC_yOKA7xE</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B\" title=\"2021 AMC 10B\">2021 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2021 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wik